{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "def change_base(x: int, base: int):\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to base.\n    return string representation after the conversion.\n    base numbers are less than 10.\n    >>> change_base(8, 3)\n    '22'\n    >>> change_base(8, 2)\n    '1000'\n    >>> change_base(7, 2)\n    '111'\n    \"\"\"\n    if x == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    result = \"\"\n    while x > 0:\n        remainder = x % base\n        result = str(remainder) + result\n        x //= base\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/45", "solution": "```python\ndef triangle_area(a, h):\n    \"\"\"Given length of a side and high return area for a triangle.\"\"\"\n    # The Triangle class encapsulates the calculation logic.\n    class Triangle:\n        def __init__(self, side_length: float, height: float):\n            self._side_length = side_length\n            self._height = height\n\n        def calculate_area(self) -> float:\n            return (self._side_length * self._height) / 2\n\n    triangle_obj = Triangle(a, h)\n    return triangle_obj.calculate_area()\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "```python\ndef fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the n-th element of the Fib4 sequence iteratively.\n    It uses a list to store intermediate results to avoid recursion and ensure efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize the list with the first four base cases\n    fib_sequence = [0, 0, 2, 0]\n\n    # Iterate from 4 up to n (inclusive)\n    for i in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib = fib_sequence[i-1] + fib_sequence[i-2] + fib_sequence[i-3] + fib_sequence[i-4]\n        fib_sequence.append(next_fib)\n\n    return fib_sequence[n]\n```"}
