{"task_id": "HumanEval/59", "solution": "```python\ndef largest_prime_factor(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Return the largest prime factor of n. Assume n > 1 and is not a prime.\n    \"\"\"\n    largest_factor = 1\n\n    # Handle factor 2: divide n by 2 until it's odd, updating largest_factor.\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        largest_factor = 2\n        n //= 2\n\n    # Iterate through odd numbers starting from 3 up to sqrt(n).\n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= n:\n        # While i divides n, update largest_factor and divide n.\n        while n % i == 0:\n            largest_factor = i\n            n //= i\n        i += 2\n\n    # If n is still greater than 2, the remaining n is the largest prime factor.\n    if n > 2:\n        largest_factor = n\n\n    return largest_factor\n```"}
