{"task_id": "HumanEval/63", "solution": "_memo = {}\n\ndef fibfib(n: int):\n    \"\"\"The FibFib number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fibfib(0) == 0\n    fibfib(1) == 0\n    fibfib(2) == 1\n    fibfib(n) == fibfib(n-1) + fibfib(n-2) + fibfib(n-3).\n    Please write a function to efficiently compute the n-th element of the fibfib number sequence.\n    >>> fibfib(1)\n    0\n    >>> fibfib(5)\n    4\n    >>> fibfib(8)\n    24\n    \"\"\"\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    if n == 0:\n        result = 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        result = 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        result = 1\n    else:\n        result = fibfib(n - 1) + fibfib(n - 2) + fibfib(n - 3)\n\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/62", "solution": "```python\nclass Polynomial:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates a polynomial's coefficients and provides the method to compute its derivative.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, coefficients: list):\n        \"\"\"Initializes a Polynomial instance with a list of coefficients.\"\"\"\n        self._coefficients = coefficients\n\n    def calculate_derivative(self) -> list:\n        \"\"\"Calculates and returns the coefficients of the derivative polynomial.\"\"\"\n        derivative_coefficients = []\n        # The derivative of c_n * x^n is n * c_n * x^(n-1).\n        # We start from the coefficient of x^1 (xs[1]) as the constant term of the derivative.\n        # The original coefficients are indexed from 0 (c0, c1, c2, ...).\n        # The derivative's first term (constant) comes from original c1.\n        # The derivative's second term (coeff of x^1) comes from original c2.\n        # So, for original coefficient xs[k], its contribution to the derivative is (k * xs[k]) for x^(k-1).\n        # This means the k-th element of the derivative list (0-indexed) comes from (k+1)-th element of original list.\n        # Its value is (k+1) * original_coefficients[k+1].\n        for i, coeff in enumerate(self._coefficients[1:]):\n            derivative_coefficients.append((i + 1) * coeff)\n        return derivative_coefficients\n\ndef derivative(xs: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    xs represent coefficients of a polynomial.\n    xs[0] + xs[1] * x + xs[2] * x^2 + ....\n    Return derivative of this polynomial in the same form.\n    \"\"\"\n    polynomial_instance = Polynomial(xs)\n    return polynomial_instance.calculate_derivative()\n```"}
